{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"05df43558261a70e","type":"group","x":1060,"y":-100,"width":3020,"height":569},
		{"id":"de08494a3b784650","type":"group","x":-280,"y":2100,"width":1232,"height":760},
		{"id":"a7e9d52d3ed4ab24","type":"group","x":-280,"y":1380,"width":1232,"height":670},
		{"id":"9456cfca523288ca","type":"group","x":-284,"y":780,"width":1224,"height":520},
		{"id":"145641da7ae98e4d","type":"group","x":-284,"y":360,"width":1224,"height":387},
		{"id":"773446d545329138","type":"group","x":-284,"y":40,"width":1224,"height":290},
		{"id":"8ef0ef1e06052473","type":"text","text":"# A Knowledge Graph of Intelligence","x":-284,"y":-100,"width":1224,"height":112,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"b15fb411d952e5d4","type":"text","text":"#### How do you define intelligence?","x":-264,"y":60,"width":520,"height":70,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"75efa8c2f712c788","type":"text","text":"_Creating a single definition of intelligence is controversial, and historically even dangerous. I will provide this definition, but it is not everyone's._\n\n**Intelligence is the ability of [[Intelligence is rapid|rapid]], [[Intelligence is fluid|fluid]], [[Intelligence is generalizable|generalizable]], [[Intelligence is durable|durable]] [[learning]].**\n","x":-264,"y":172,"width":520,"height":148},
		{"id":"a391b0e0c3ba5284","type":"text","text":"#### How does intelligence develop?","x":-264,"y":800,"width":520,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"e496190cd4894a5c","type":"file","file":"👶 How does intelligence develop?/👶 The newborn brain.md","x":411,"y":830,"width":509,"height":212},
		{"id":"434b0362993b6264","type":"text","text":"The structure of a brain determines how it develops.","x":-264,"y":936,"width":520,"height":64},
		{"id":"6df29405a5fe628e","type":"text","text":"... but also, the structure of the body determines how intelligence develops.","x":-260,"y":1100,"width":512,"height":115},
		{"id":"af443f81c4f60eb0","type":"file","file":"How do we define intelligence?.md","x":380,"y":162,"width":540,"height":168},
		{"id":"c0da5ecdc889ab6e","type":"text","text":"#### What is intelligence made of?\n","x":-260,"y":1400,"width":520,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"7182cc7256920fa8","type":"file","file":"🤖 What are we missing about intelligence?/embodied cognition.md","x":405,"y":1100,"width":515,"height":180},
		{"id":"8b5555ec04bfbe10","type":"text","text":"... and where is it, in humans?","x":415,"y":1460,"width":517,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"1be3014bef8c4f12","type":"file","file":"🧠 Where is intelligence located?/Structures comprising the brain/lobe.md","x":419,"y":1560,"width":509,"height":160},
		{"id":"7c89e4022dc01c20","type":"text","text":"#### Why do we define intelligence?","x":-264,"y":380,"width":520,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"952d140b446dff2c","type":"file","file":"🧠 Where is intelligence located?/🧠 What is the substance of intelligence?.md","x":404,"y":1790,"width":520,"height":240},
		{"id":"2ff1841878e10c6c","type":"text","text":"Intelligence can exist in many different ways, and there has been extensive debate about whether human intelligence is strictly due to the capabilities of neurons (see: connectionist versus symbolic AI)","x":-260,"y":1600,"width":520,"height":140},
		{"id":"bdfc4de02ae92b5e","type":"text","text":"... but providing a single definition introduces the threat of bias.","x":409,"y":440,"width":511,"height":50,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"bdf010d2da5b4df5","type":"text","text":"Structure is extremely important in the functioning and success of an intelligent system. Could we better understand what structures are more intelligent that others?","x":-187,"y":1906,"width":455,"height":124},
		{"id":"7d6d450f7274ed04","type":"text","text":"> “Every aspect of learning or any other feature of intelligence can in principle be so precisely described that a machine can be made to simulate it.”\n\n  \n— John McCarthy et al., \"A Proposal for the Dartmouth Summer Research Project on Artificial Intelligence,\" 1955","x":-264,"y":480,"width":520,"height":123},
		{"id":"76acdc4ceb351ea3","type":"text","text":"We define intelligence so we may create systems that solve problems intelligently.","x":-140,"y":640,"width":272,"height":87},
		{"id":"329410afea4b97a1","type":"text","text":"Real, tangible harm is possible when we exclude, prioritize, or dehumanize people based off a motivated definition of intelligence. [[@gebruOxfordHandbookAI2019|(Gebru, 2019)]]","x":411,"y":580,"width":509,"height":121},
		{"id":"567d9413fe304df2","type":"text","text":"#### What is still unknown about intelligence?","x":-252,"y":2120,"width":520,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"21a76dfccc8f5168","type":"file","file":"🤖 What are we missing about intelligence?/🤖What open questions remain in intelligence?.md","x":404,"y":2150,"width":520,"height":690},
		{"id":"be1403a61da55708","type":"text","text":"There is far more to be learned about intelligence than is currently known, as the understanding of the mind from a neurocognitive basis is only a few centuries old, dating back to the mid-19th century.","x":-252,"y":2240,"width":520,"height":120},
		{"id":"f7c05e04ea5c7eed","type":"text","text":"There is continuous and myriad research into various structures that enable artificial intelligence. However, some of the most obvious contemporary failings in neuroscience are the failure to encode memory for easy access and to do so de novo in an efficient way. This leaves us with an overall question: can we continue to understand the human brain better and implement those learnings into artificial intelligence?","x":-252,"y":2420,"width":520,"height":200},
		{"id":"a2ef87a34e6f5a4b","type":"file","file":"unimal.png","x":-250,"y":2630,"width":291,"height":210},
		{"id":"a838a3cba973738b","type":"file","file":"🎓 What are the features of intelligence?/Intelligence is rapid.md","x":1080,"y":-69,"width":656,"height":171},
		{"id":"f7cfe9a022000506","type":"file","file":"🎓 What are the features of intelligence?/Intelligence is fluid.md","x":1820,"y":-69,"width":656,"height":171},
		{"id":"2732c18016d8eb6e","type":"file","file":"🎓 What are the features of intelligence?/Intelligence is generalizable.md","x":2580,"y":-72,"width":678,"height":174},
		{"id":"c3b23fe1e1c66f60","type":"file","file":"🎓 What are the features of intelligence?/Intelligence is durable.md","x":3380,"y":-69,"width":678,"height":171},
		{"id":"8106bf469fe7e88f","type":"file","file":"infant learning.png","x":1948,"y":142,"width":400,"height":303},
		{"id":"a6997a18a60637ee","type":"file","file":"🤖 What are we missing about intelligence?/Frostbite score per game experience.png","x":1189,"y":142,"width":438,"height":303},
		{"id":"9124f19182122a55","type":"file","file":"slime maze.png","x":2705,"y":160,"width":428,"height":285},
		{"id":"0ec88752e49c01b5","type":"file","file":"classes trained.png","x":3467,"y":160,"width":504,"height":285},
		{"id":"c2d0648823d44250","type":"text","text":"What's the best body plan for each unimal? And inversely: how does the body plan drive learning?","x":80,"y":2700,"width":250,"height":105}
	],
